## Minimal Harness workflow

This repository uses `.harness/` as the task and verification source of truth. At the start of every session, run `python3 .harness/harness.py doctor`, then `python3 .harness/harness.py status`, and read `.harness/HANDOFF.md`. Resume a task that is `in_progress`. If it is `blocked`, report the blocker and obtain the needed intervention, then use `unblock` before mutating the project. Run `python3 .harness/harness.py next` only when status shows no active or blocked task.

Keep one writer in the shared workspace. Run command acceptance with `verify`. Actually perform browser and manual checks before using `record`; code inspection or an unavailable tool is not proof. Run `complete` only after every acceptance item and policy gate passes. Changes made after verification require fresh evidence. Respect `allowed_paths` and operations in `approval_required_operations`, while preserving authorization the user already granted instead of asking twice. At every stopping or transfer point, run `python3 .harness/harness.py handoff` before another writer takes over.
